Renode sim of the ScanWatch 2 (HWA10) firmware. See NOTES.md for status.

Prereqs (not in the repo — supply your own):
  - external_flash.bin : an 8 MB dump of the watch's external SPI flash, placed
    in renode-sim/ (git-ignored; contains the association secret — never commit).
  - Renode (tested v1.17.0). Put `renode` on your PATH, or use its full path below.
  - The firmware package `hwa10_3411_Tf4fD4.bin` in the repo root (one level up).
  - NRF52840.svd in this directory (Nordic's official SVD, the copy Renode's own
    nrf52840 platform uses). Fetch it:
      cd renode-sim
      wget -qO- https://dl.antmicro.com/projects/renode/svd/NRF52840.svd.gz | gunzip > NRF52840.svd

Run everything from this directory (scripts use paths relative to it):
  cd renode-sim
Keep Renode's stdin open when scripting it (e.g. `renode ... < <(sleep 1000)`):
with `< /dev/null` its console thread spins on EOF and leaks ~20 MB/s of host
memory for as long as the process lives. Run one instance at a time from this
directory (they share out/).

Rebuild the flash image from the firmware package:
  python3 extract.py

Boot (headless):
  renode --disable-xwt --console -e "include @boot.resc; start"

Boot with readable wlog (Phase 0 gate — applies the documented shortcuts):
  renode --disable-xwt --console -e "include @run-logs.resc"
  Prints:  [M] boot / [M] rtc_value : 0 / [M] HWA10 boot reason = 0

Coverage progress bar (native trace, not slow Python hooks):
  renode --disable-xwt --console -e "include @trace.resc"
  python3 coverage.py /tmp/hwa10_trace.bin.gz
  -> known functions in first-execution order + the loop the boot ends stuck in.
  (Renode writes trace output relative to ITS cwd, so trace.resc uses /tmp.)

Files:
  mkdis.sh      builds out/appl.dis and out/sd.dis (absolute flash addresses)
  calltrace.py  emits hooks that print the first entry into every callee of a code
                range; how the boot's stall points were found (needs out/appl.dis)
  extract.py    rebuilds appl.bin/bl.bin/sd.bin/flash.bin from the package
  hwa10.repl    nrf52840 platform (stock Renode + local SVD applied in boot.resc)
  boot.resc     load flash + boot from MBR@0x0, UART capture to out/
  run-logs.resc Phase 0 gate: boot with shortcuts, prints readable wlog
  trace.resc    capture a boot PC trace for coverage.py (native ExecutionTracer)
  coverage.py   offline progress bar: maps a trace against symbols.txt
  symbols.txt   address -> name map (naming source for the progress bar)
  logs.resc     boot + hooks on the 5 wlog formatters (for post-wedge logs)
  NRF52840.svd  peripheral SVD (local, avoids per-run download)

Current status: Phase 0 gate ACHIEVED (readable wlog). The first blocker was a
HardFault in sd_mbr_command (svc #24), patched to return success; the wlog ring
is force-drained. Boot then stops at driver-completion semaphore waits that need
the RTOS scheduler/tick (interrupts). NOTES.md has the full diagnosis, the
"Fidelity gaps" ledger, and the next step for Phases 1/2.
